# US-034 spike inventory: tmux commands issued by Claude Code agent teams
# os: Linux 7.2.8-200.fc44.x86_64 x86_64 (Fedora 44), run 2026-10-03
# claude: 2.1.288 (Claude Code), launched interactive with --teammate-mode tmux --model haiku --dangerously-skip-permissions
# env: CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1 TMUX=/tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock,4242,0 TMUX_PANE=%0, logging fake tmux first on PATH
# prompt: two haiku teammates each send "ok" to the lead, then the lead shuts them down and cleans up the team
# fake replies: -V "tmux 3.5a"; display-message #{pane_id} %0, #{window_id} @0; list-panes lists %0 plus live teammate panes;
#   split-window/new-window/new-session print the next %N; respawn-pane runs the command in a PTY; everything else prints nothing, exit 0
# lines: CALL (caller env), argv (shell-quoted), stdin (when any), out (stdout returned), respawn (decoded command), exit
# concurrent calls interleaved two log lines, kept raw: the "argv:  argv:" line holds two kill-pane calls,
#   kill-pane -t %1 and kill-pane -t %2, each prefixed by -S /tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock; the argv line ending in
#   "exit: 0" continues on the next line as set-option -p -t %1 remain-on-exit failed
# redactions: <cwd> scratch workdir, <claude-exec> Claude executable path, session-<id8> team name, <session-uuid> parent session id
#
# distinct sub-command forms (observed unless marked static; static = present in the 2.1.288 bundle, reached only outside tmux):
#  1 -V                                                     static, isAvailable() checks exit code 0 only, no version parsing
#  2 display-message -p #{client_termtype}                  startup probe, leader
#  3 display-message [-t <pane>] -p #{window_id}|#{pane_id} leader window and pane lookup (#{pane_id} only when TMUX_PANE is unset)
#  4 show-environment -g                                    startup probe, leader
#  5 show -Av mouse                                         startup probe, leader and every teammate
#  6 show -gv focus-events                                  startup probe, leader and every teammate
#  7 list-panes -t <window> -F #{pane_id}
#  8 split-window -d -t <pane> -h -l 70% -P -F #{pane_id} -- cat   first teammate
#  9 split-window -d -t <pane> -v|-h -P -F #{pane_id} -- cat       next teammates
# 10 set-option -p -t <pane> <option> <value>   options: window-style, pane-border-style, pane-active-border-style, pane-border-format, remain-on-exit
# 11 set-option -w -t <window> pane-border-status top
# 12 select-pane -t <pane> -T <title>
# 13 respawn-pane -k -t <pane> -- <sh command>   cd <cwd> && env CLAUDECODE=1 CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1 <claude-exec> --agent-id ... --team-name ...
# 14 select-layout -t <window> main-vertical
# 15 resize-pane -t <pane> -x 30%
# 16 kill-pane -t <pane>
# 17 has-session -t claude-swarm                                     static, -L claude-swarm-<pid>
# 18 new-session -d -s claude-swarm -n swarm-view -P -F #{pane_id} -- cat   static, -L claude-swarm-<pid>
# 19 new-window -t claude-swarm -n swarm-view -P -F #{pane_id} -- cat      static, -L claude-swarm-<pid>
# 20 list-windows -t claude-swarm -F #{window_name}                  static, -L claude-swarm-<pid>
#    plus select-layout -t <window> tiled (static, form 14)
# global flags: -S <socket> taken from the first comma field of TMUX inside tmux; -L claude-swarm-<pid> outside tmux
# control mode -C: never used. send-keys: never used (teammate commands go through respawn-pane)
# cmux comparison (/home/arthur/dev/cmux @ ecba57ac71, CLI/cmux.swift:26915 runTmuxCompat switch): every verb above is in
#   cmux's tmux compat except show-environment, which cmux does not list. cmux also answers select-window, kill-window,
#   capture-pane, rename-window, wait-for, last-pane, show-buffer, save-buffer, last-window, next-window, previous-window,
#   set-hook, set-buffer, list-buffers, source-file, refresh-client, attach-session and detach-client, none of which
#   Claude Code 2.1.288 issued here, so Paneflow's shim leaves them out
#
CALL TMUX=/tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock\,4242\,0 TMUX_PANE=%0
  argv: show -Av mouse
  exit: 0
CALL TMUX=/tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock\,4242\,0 TMUX_PANE=%0
  argv: show -gv focus-events
  exit: 0
CALL TMUX=/tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock\,4242\,0 TMUX_PANE=%0
  argv: display-message -p \#\{client_termtype\}
  out: ''
  exit: 0
CALL TMUX=/tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock\,4242\,0 TMUX_PANE=%0
  argv: show-environment -g
  exit: 0
CALL TMUX=/tmp/pf-fake-tmux.sock\,4242\,0 TMUX_PANE=%0
  argv: display-message -p \#\{client_termtype\}
